cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Driven States Registry and Reactive Periodic Table
message: If you use this dataset or software, please cite it as below.
type: dataset
authors:
  - given-names: Daniel
    family-names: Leonforte
    affiliation: Eigenart Filmproduktion, Wiesbaden, Germany
repository-code: "https://github.com/dl-eigenart/driven-states-registry"
url: "https://dl-eigenart.github.io/driven-states-registry/"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-20"
license: CC-BY-4.0
license-url: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
abstract: >-
  An openly graded registry of material states that exist only while a drive is
  running - light-induced phases and Floquet-engineered bands - together with a
  machine-readable description layer for the controllability of matter. Version
  0.1.0 records 82 driven states across 58 host materials from six domains, each
  with drive parameters, lifetime, mechanism, an explicit evidence level and a
  primary source with DOI. Compilation was AI-assisted under human direction and
  checked against primary literature; no entry has been reviewed by a domain
  expert.
keywords:
  - Floquet engineering
  - light-induced superconductivity
  - photoinduced phase transition
  - charge density wave
  - non-equilibrium materials
  - materials database
  - FAIR data
